    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d516">

                <pb facs="0670" n="560" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg560"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/2981</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Ministry of Foreign
                            Affairs at Nanking to the Chinese
                            Legation</hi><anchor n="94" xml:id="d516-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-11-24">November 24, 1931</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Lately Japanese have been intensely circulating news that the Chinese troops at
                    Chinchow will attack the Japanese troops and Chang Hsueh-Liang will declare war.
                    Japan’s intention is to launch immediate attack upon Chinchow. According to
                    railway reports Japanese gunboat <hi rendition="#italic">Kuoa</hi> arrived 23rd
                    declaring to protect wireless station but evidently to help attack Chinchow.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d516-f1" n="94" type="source" xml:id="d516-f1-content">
                <p>Copy of telegram handed by the First Secretary of the Chinese Legation to Mr.
                    Hansford S. Miller of the Division of Far Eastern Affairs on November 25,
                    1931.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
